==English==

===Etymology===
{{uder|en|la|-}} third-person singular subjunctive of {{m|la|exeō||depart}} used as an impersonal imperative, literally “let him go forth”.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[license]] or [[permit]] for [[absence]] from a [[university]] or a [[religious]] [[house]] (such as a [[monastery]]).
#: {{cot|en|absit}}
# A [[permission]] which a [[bishop]] [[grant]]s to a [[priest]] to go out of his [[diocese]].
# {{lb|en|dated|UK}} Leave of absence from a [[public school]] or college.
#*'''1984''', {{w|Anita Brookner}}, ''Hotel du Lac'', Penguin 2016, p. 66:
#*:[I]t was impossible to imagine her doing anything except eating ice-cream and smoking, like a child on an '''exeat''' from school.
# {{lb|en|obsolete|theatre}} A stage direction to leave the stage.
#: {{cot|en|exeunt|q=plural form}}

